The GPL-3.0-or-later parts remain GPL-3.0-or-later. GPLv3 section 13 expressly permits
combining a GPL-covered work with AGPLv3 work and conveying the result, with AGPL section
13's network-interaction requirement applying to the combination. That is the arrangement
here, and it is the same one pdn-soundmodem itself already runs on.

Provenance
----------

The modem core contains work derived from QtSoundModem (GPLv3+, (c) Andrei Kopanchuk UZ7HO,
ported to C++/Qt by John Wiseman G8BPQ) and from Dire Wolf (GPL-2.0-or-later, (c) John
Langner WB2OSZ). Individual algorithms name their source in the comments of the C# they were
ported into. The FEC and protocol layers are implemented from the published specifications
(IL2P v0.6, FX.25) against those specifications' own test vectors.

Corresponding source
--------------------

Everything in this package other than the .NET runtime is built from
https://github.com/packet-net/pdn-soundmodem, at the tag matching this package's version, and
from the M0LTE.* packages named above, whose sources are linked from their NuGet listings. The
.NET runtime's source is at https://github.com/dotnet/runtime.
